:: NPC - leave husband [no-redirect]

<!-- #### npc_leave_husband.jpg | two people in a quiet post-apocalyptic cabin room, intimate conversation, warm dim light, serious mood --ar 4:2 --p -->
<center>
    <<actionImage $tmpGirl approach>>
</center>
<br />

<<set _rel = $tmpGirl.relationship ?? 0>>
<<set _corruption = $tmpGirl.corruption ?? 0>>
<<set _husbandName = setup.getNpcById($tmpGirl.family.husband)?.name ?? 'her husband'>>

You steered the conversation toward <<=_husbandName>>. Not accusingly — just asking how things really were between them. Whether she was happy.
<br /><br />

<<if _rel >= 80>>

She was quiet for a moment. Something shifted in her expression.
<br /><br />

<<if _rel >= 90 || _corruption >= 50>>
<<sayNpc $tmpGirl>>
    Honestly? It's not what I thought it would be. I don't know anymore.
<</sayNpc>>
<<else>>
<<sayNpc $tmpGirl>>
    That's... a complicated question.
<</sayNpc>>
<</if>>
<br />
She didn't walk away.
<br /><br />

<div id="lh_push">
<<linkreplace 'Tell her you want her for yourself'>>
    <<run $('#lh_leave').hide()>>
    You said it plainly — that you wanted her here, with you. Not just as a guest passing through.
    <br /><br />
    <<set _leaveChance = Math.min(_rel - 40 + Math.floor(_corruption / 2), 90)>>
    <<if setup.percentageChance(_leaveChance)>>
        She looked at you for a long moment. Then something in her settled.
        <br /><br />
        <<sayNpc $tmpGirl>>
            I've been telling myself it's fine. It's not fine. I'll end it with him.
        <</sayNpc>>
        <br />
        She said it quietly, like a decision she'd already been building to.
        <br /><br />
        <<include 'NPC end marriage - finalize'>>
        <<set $guests[$guestId] = $tmpGirl>>
        <strong>(Marriage ended)</strong>
    <<else>>
        She looked at you. Then at the floor.
        <br /><br />
        <<sayNpc $tmpGirl>>
            I... I can't. It's not that simple. I'm sorry.
        <</sayNpc>>
        <br />
        She seemed genuinely torn about it, which was something.
        <br /><br />
        <<set $tmpGirl.relationship = Math.max(_rel - 3, -100)>>
        <<set $guests[$guestId] = $tmpGirl>>
        <strong>(Relationship − 3)</strong>
    <</if>>
    <br /><br />
    <<link 'Back'>>
        <<if $tmpGirlViewBack>><<goto $tmpGirlViewBack>><<else>><<goto 'NPC view - guest'>><</if>>
    <</link>>
<</linkreplace>>
</div>
<div id="lh_leave">
<<link 'Leave it alone'>>
    <<if $tmpGirlViewBack>><<goto $tmpGirlViewBack>><<else>><<goto 'NPC view - guest'>><</if>>
<</link>>
</div>

<<else>>

<<sayNpc $tmpGirl>>
    My marriage is my business. But... thank you for asking.
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
She wasn't offended. If anything, she seemed a little flattered that someone cared enough to ask.
<br /><br />
<<set $tmpGirl.happy = Math.min(($tmpGirl.happy ?? 0) + 2, 100)>>
<<set $guests[$guestId] = $tmpGirl>>
<strong>(Happy + 2)</strong>
<br /><br />
<<link 'Back'>>
    <<if $tmpGirlViewBack>><<goto $tmpGirlViewBack>><<else>><<goto 'NPC view - guest'>><</if>>
<</link>>

<</if>>
